# armour/man/scale: scale armour on the man (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2 / 25.3 / 27.4: the Imperial T3 and the finer cut
# of mail): rows of 3 px scales, each with a step-3 top and a step-1 lower edge on the lit side (step 2 / 1 on the shadow
# side), the courses offset so they read as scallops, never as stripes or dither; a steel gorget, a belt, a solid band hem.
# Medium weight: the civilian silhouette plus the tassets (scale_hang) and the shoulders (shared/pauldron_scale*).
# Finish regions: R the gorget's rim and the hem band, P the lit chest, G the chest socket, N the lowest course, W a 2x2
# spot on the shadow side. Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py (fill: scale).
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) a step-4 specular on the lit top of the first scales / lames / plates (top-left light):
# with no step 4 a coloured alloy read as clay; the glint and the dark core make any metal read as metal.
use person
body man
role armour scale
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

